<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default">
<!--
    GH-2786: "Decompiler produces incorrect syntax with double negation"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/2786

    Two nested float negations (FLOAT_NEG of FLOAT_NEG, deliberately NOT folded
    by analysis for NaN/sign correctness) must render as -(-x).  The pre-fix
    upstream decompiler emitted the adjacent token pair "minus minus x" (no parentheses), which C re-parses
    as the pre-decrement operator: wrong semantics from valid-looking source.

    The fix lives in PrintLanguage::parentheses (printlanguage.cc), unary_prefix
    case: a unary prefix token nested directly inside the same unary prefix
    token always gets parentheses.  This fork already carries that fix, so
    there is no option to toggle; this datatest is the regression guard ported
    from kuna's tests/stages/gh2786-unaryspacing.xml (GayHydra #477).
    Assertion #1 proves the fixed form; assertion #2 proves the mis-parsing
    token never appears.

    Bytes: the issue's MIPS:BE:32 function (LukeSerne's attachment) with a
    trailing "jr ra; nop" appended so flow analysis terminates in the image.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0" readonly="true">
c7a2007c460004874406a00046009207
46001087440540004407100027ae00dc
27af00d827b900d4e7a00078afb90018
afaf0014afae0010e7a200480c0053b4
27a4008403e0000800000000
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x0" name="FUN_00000000"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu FUN_00000000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH2786 #1: nested float negation is parenthesized" min="1" max="1">-\(-\w+\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH2786 #2: the mis-parsing predecrement token is gone" min="0" max="0">--\w</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
